  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The spin-only magnetic moment value of the most basic oxide of vanadium among <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is____B.M. (Nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the most basic oxide among the given oxides.</p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, Vanadium is in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;oxidation state</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired electrons are there,</p><p>Its magnetic moment is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>83</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8771;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></math></p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;number of unpaired electrons)</p>",
